meta {
  name: Newsletter - Subscribe
  type: http
  seq: 81
}

post {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/newsletter
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "someone@example.com",
    "turnstileToken": "XXXX.DUMMY.TOKEN.XXXX",
    "website": ""
  }
}

docs {
  Public endpoint for the newsletter form of the footer (#938), rate limited (5 requests per minute per IP address).
  It fails while the instance has no EMAILOCTOPUS_NEWSLETTER_LIST_ID: the footer then shows no form.
  `turnstileToken` comes from the Cloudflare Turnstile widget. With the Cloudflare test secret key, the dummy token passes.
  `website` is the honeypot field: it must stay empty.
}
